A||||2||MIKLAV||V-6 Engine Running Lean||||1
Z||000000||MIKLAV||10-09-1999||11:29 AM||||Techincal question.  What does it mean when I put the ECM into the Diagonistic mode while the engines running and the "Service Engine Soon" dash light flashes once per second.  I read the manual it tell me that the engine is in a "closed loop" and running lean.  I checked the timing and minor adjustments but still the light flashes.  Is there another adjustment I can make or possibly a defective sensor?<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||Lynx||10-09-1999||01:45 PM||||It should flash 4 times then pause then flash 4 times again. Thats the lean code for both engines. Well if it is running lean your best bet is a ground, vaccum leak, or the O2 sensor. Yes it can be the O2 sensor even if it dosent show a code for the O2 actually most of the time when the O2 is bad it shows lean air, and it makes the car actually run real rich. So if at idle the car is starting to idle bad and there is a black smoke coming out of the exhaust its probably the O2.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||10-09-1999||04:38 PM||||This "rough" determination of the air/fuel ratio is actually a function of how long the light stays on vs. how long it is off.  The frequency of the flashes will only indicate the mode the ECM is presently in. I would say (from your description) that everything is just fine..<P>Mike||||reg||1
